{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"The React Foundation announcement was published on October 7, 2025, authored by Seth Webster, Matt Carroll, Joe Savona, and Sophie Alpert.","source_span":"October 7, 2025 by Seth Webster, Matt Carroll, Joe Savona, Sophie Alpert"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"React was open sourced over a decade before this announcement.","source_span":"We open sourced React over a decade ago to help developers build great user experiences."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"React and React Native are being moved from Meta to a new React Foundation.","source_span":"we are announcing our plans to move React and React Native from Meta to a new React Foundation"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"A new independent technical governance structure will be implemented alongside the move to the React Foundation.","source_span":"As a part of this change, we will also be implementing a new independent technical governance structure."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"The React Foundation will be the new home for React, React Native, and supporting projects like JSX.","source_span":"We will make the React Foundation the new home for React, React Native, and some supporting projects like JSX."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"The React Foundation will maintain React's infrastructure (GitHub, CI, trademarks), organize React Conf, and create ecosystem support initiatives such as financial support, grants, and programs.","source_span":"Maintain React's infrastructure like GitHub, CI, and trademarks... Organize React Conf... Create initiatives to support the React ecosystem like financial support of ecosystem projects, issuing grants, and creating programs"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"The React Foundation will be governed by a board of directors, with Seth Webster serving as the executive director.","source_span":"The React Foundation will be governed by a board of directors, with Seth Webster serving as the executive director."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"The founding corporate members of the React Foundation are Amazon, Callstack, Expo, Meta, Microsoft, Software Mansion, and Vercel.","source_span":"The founding corporate members of the React Foundation will be Amazon, Callstack, Expo, Meta, Microsoft, Software Mansion, and Vercel."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"React's new technical governance structure will be independent from the React Foundation, ensuring no single company is overrepresented.","source_span":"we plan to define a new technical governance structure for React that is independent from the React Foundation"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","statement":"The React team will reach out to the community for feedback on the new technical governance structure and share details in a future post once finalized.","source_span":"we will reach out to the community for feedback. Once finalized, we will share details in a future post."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","fact_refs":[7],"question":"Who are the founding corporate members of the React Foundation?","answer":"The founding corporate members are Amazon, Callstack, Expo, Meta, Microsoft, Software Mansion, and Vercel."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","fact_refs":[6],"question":"Who will serve as executive director of the React Foundation?","answer":"Seth Webster will serve as the executive director of the React Foundation's board of directors."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What projects will become the new home under the React Foundation?","answer":"The React Foundation will be the new home for React, React Native, and supporting projects like JSX."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What responsibilities will the React Foundation take on?","answer":"It will maintain React's infrastructure (GitHub, CI, trademarks), organize React Conf, and create ecosystem initiatives such as financial support, grants, and programs."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","fact_refs":[2,3],"question":"What organizational change was announced for React and React Native, and what accompanies it?","answer":"React and React Native are moving from Meta to a new React Foundation, accompanied by a new independent technical governance structure."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","fact_refs":[8],"question":"How does React's new technical governance structure relate to the React Foundation?","answer":"The new technical governance structure will be independent from the React Foundation, ensuring no single company or organization is overrepresented."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_introducing-the-react-foundation","fact_refs":[9],"question":"What will happen before React's new technical governance structure is finalized?","answer":"The React team will reach out to the community for feedback, and once finalized, will share details in a future post."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"React Compiler 1.0 became available on October 7, 2025.","source_span":"Oct 7, 2025... React Compiler 1.0 is available today."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"Compiler-powered lint rules ship in eslint-plugin-react-hooks's recommended and recommended-latest presets.","source_span":"Compiler-powered lint rules ship in `eslint-plugin-react-hooks`'s `recommended` and `recommended-latest` preset."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"The React team published an incremental adoption guide and partnered with Expo, Vite, and Next.js so new apps can start with the compiler enabled.","source_span":"We've published an incremental adoption guide, and partnered with Expo, Vite, and Next.js so new apps can start with the compiler enabled."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"React Compiler works on both React and React Native and automatically optimizes components and hooks without requiring rewrites.","source_span":"React Compiler works on both React and React Native, and automatically optimizes components and hooks without requiring rewrites."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"The compiler has been battle tested on major apps at Meta and is fully production-ready.","source_span":"The compiler has been battle tested on major apps at Meta and is fully production-ready."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"React Compiler's first beta was published the year before this 1.0 release (linked as 2024/10/21).","source_span":"Last year, we published React Compiler's first beta"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"The React team's first exploration into compilers started with Prepack in 2017.","source_span":"The React team's first exploration into compilers started with Prepack in 2017."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"In 2021, Xuan Huang demoed the first iteration of the new React Compiler.","source_span":"In 2021, Xuan Huang demoed the first iteration of a new take on React Compiler."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"Joe Savona, Sathya Gunasekaran, Mofei Zhang, and Lauren Tan worked through the compiler's first rewrite, moving its architecture to a Control Flow Graph (CFG) based High-Level Intermediate Representation (HIR).","source_span":"Joe Savona, Sathya Gunasekaran, Mofei Zhang, and Lauren Tan worked through our first rewrite, moving the compiler's architecture into a Control Flow Graph (CFG) based High-Level Intermediate Representation (HIR)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"To install React Compiler via npm, run: npm install --save-dev --save-exact babel-plugin-react-compiler@latest.","source_span":"npm install --save-dev --save-exact babel-plugin-react-compiler@latest"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"React Compiler now supports optional chains and array indices as dependencies, resulting in fewer re-renders and more responsive UIs.","source_span":"React Compiler now supports optional chains and array indices as dependencies. These improvements ultimately result in fewer re-renders and more responsive UIs"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"At Meta Quest Store, the compiler improved initial loads and cross-page navigations by up to 12%, with certain interactions more than 2.5x faster, while memory usage stayed neutral.","source_span":"We've seen initial loads and cross-page navigations improve by up to 12%, while certain interactions are more than 2.5× faster. Memory usage stays neutral even with these wins."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","statement":"React Compiler is compatible with React 17 and up.","source_span":"React Compiler is compatible with React 17 and up."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","fact_refs":[0],"question":"When did React Compiler 1.0 become available?","answer":"React Compiler 1.0 became available on October 7, 2025."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","fact_refs":[2],"question":"Which frameworks has the React team partnered with to help new apps adopt React Compiler by default?","answer":"The React team partnered with Expo, Vite, and Next.js so new apps can start with the compiler enabled, alongside publishing an incremental adoption guide."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","fact_refs":[11],"question":"What performance improvements did React Compiler bring to the Meta Quest Store app?","answer":"Initial loads and cross-page navigations improved by up to 12%, certain interactions became more than 2.5x faster, and memory usage stayed neutral."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","fact_refs":[12],"question":"Which React versions is React Compiler backwards compatible with?","answer":"React Compiler is compatible with React 17 and up."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","fact_refs":[8],"question":"Who worked on the first rewrite of React Compiler's architecture into a CFG-based HIR?","answer":"Joe Savona, Sathya Gunasekaran, Mofei Zhang, and Lauren Tan worked through the first rewrite, moving the compiler's architecture into a Control Flow Graph (CFG) based High-Level Intermediate Representation (HIR)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","fact_refs":[9],"question":"What npm command installs React Compiler's babel plugin?","answer":"Run `npm install --save-dev --save-exact babel-plugin-react-compiler@latest`."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-compiler-1","fact_refs":[6,7],"question":"What was the React team's first exploration into compilers, and who demoed the first iteration of the new React Compiler in 2021?","answer":"The team's first exploration was Prepack, started in 2017; in 2021, Xuan Huang demoed the first iteration of the new React Compiler."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"React Conf 2025 was held on October 7-8, 2025, in Henderson, Nevada.","source_span":"React Conf 2025 was held on October 7-8, 2025, in Henderson, Nevada."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"In the day 1 keynote, Mofei Zhang highlighted new React 19.2 features including Activity, useEffectEvent, Performance Tracks, and Partial Pre-Rendering.","source_span":"Mofei Zhang highlighted the new features in React 19.2 including: <Activity />... useEffectEvent... Performance Tracks... Partial Pre-Rendering"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Jack Pope announced new Canary features including <ViewTransition /> and Fragment Refs.","source_span":"Jack Pope announced new features in Canary including: <ViewTransition />... Fragment Refs"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Lauren Tan announced React Compiler v1.0 at React Conf 2025 and recommended all apps use React Compiler.","source_span":"Lauren Tan announced React Compiler v1.0 and recommended all apps use React Compiler"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Seth Webster announced the React Foundation at React Conf 2025 to steward React's open source development and community.","source_span":"Seth Webster announced the React Foundation to steward React's open source development and community."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Jorge Cohen and Nicola Corti highlighted React Native's growth of 4M weekly downloads, a 100% year-over-year increase, at the day 2 keynote.","source_span":"Jorge Cohen and Nicola Corti kicked off day 2 highlighting React Native's incredible growth with 4M weekly downloads (100% growth YoY)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Notable React Native app migrations mentioned included Shopify, Zalando, and HelloFresh, plus award-winning apps RISE, RUNNA, and Partyful, and AI apps from Mistral, Replit, and v0.","source_span":"some notable app migrations from Shopify, Zalando, and HelloFresh, award-winning apps like RISE, RUNNA, and Partyful, and AI apps from Mistral, Replit, and v0"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Riccardo Cipolleschi announced that React Native 0.82 will be New Architecture only, plus experimental Hermes V1 support.","source_span":"Riccardo Cipolleschi shared two major announcements for React Native: React Native 0.82 will be New Architecture only... Experimental Hermes V1 support"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Ruben Norte and Alex Hunt announced new web-aligned DOM APIs and new Performance APIs including a network panel and desktop app for React Native.","source_span":"Ruben Norte and Alex Hunt finished out the keynote by announcing: New web-aligned DOM APIs... New Performance APIs with a new network panel and desktop app."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","statement":"Luna Wei introduced Virtual View, a new primitive for lists in React Native that manages visibility with mode-based rendering (hidden/pre-render/visible).","source_span":"Luna Wei introduced Virtual View, a new primitive for lists that manages visibility with mode-based rendering (hidden/pre-render/visible)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","fact_refs":[0],"question":"When and where was React Conf 2025 held?","answer":"React Conf 2025 was held on October 7-8, 2025, in Henderson, Nevada."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What new React 19.2 features did Mofei Zhang highlight at React Conf 2025?","answer":"She highlighted <Activity />, useEffectEvent, Performance Tracks, and Partial Pre-Rendering."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What React Native growth statistics did Jorge Cohen and Nicola Corti present in the day 2 keynote?","answer":"They highlighted React Native's growth to 4M weekly downloads, a 100% year-over-year increase."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What major announcement did Riccardo Cipolleschi make about React Native 0.82?","answer":"He announced that React Native 0.82 will be New Architecture only, along with experimental Hermes V1 support."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-conf-2025-recap","fact_refs":[9],"question":"Who introduced Virtual View at React Conf 2025, and what does it do?","answer":"Luna Wei introduced Virtual View, a new list primitive that manages visibility with mode-based rendering (hidden/pre-render/visible)."}
